# Licences for v2.0.0

The authors have approved version v2.0.0 and the following grants for material they own and have the right to license. The final GitHub main push is authorized; a tag, GitHub Release, Zenodo archive and journal submission require separate authorization.

1. **MIT** applies to author-owned revised Python software in src/ and scripts/, software configuration and associated author-written software/reproduction documentation. The grant and copyright notice are in licenses/MIT.txt. The pre-existing licenses/HISTORICAL_CODE_LICENSE.txt is preserved verbatim and remains applicable within its original scope.
2. **Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)** applies to author-original main figures, Supporting Figures, their author-written captions, manuscript tables, Supporting Tables and shareable author-generated statistical results and plotted statistical outputs. The authors license those contributions under https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/; the complete legal text is in licenses/CC-BY-4.0.txt. Attribute the seven authors in CITATION.cff, the study title, v2.0.0, the repository and the actual version DOI once assigned; retain source credits and identify modifications.
3. **Third-party exceptions.** No MIT or CC BY grant is made over EIA, NBS, Customs or other provider observations, original exports, complete mixed monthly observation tables, source quotations, third-party software, trademarks or other material the authors cannot license. The included FRED/Board EXCHUS observations retain their upstream public-domain status with citation requested; this is not an author relicensing. EIA/NBS/Customs exports and mixed monthly inputs are excluded from the v2.0.0 file tree. Obtain necessary observations through DATA_SOURCES.md. Exceptions also apply to provider material in historical commits, which this release does not relicense.

The exact file categories and limits are recorded in licenses/FILE_LICENSES.csv and metadata/public_file_manifest.csv. Licence-text and third-party notice files retain their own terms. No blanket repository-wide CC BY or MIT grant overrides those scopes. Dependency notices remain in licenses/DEPENDENCY_LICENSES.md. A specific employer, institutional or other conflicting right, if established, must be resolved for that object; no such conflict was identified in the targeted release preparation.
